<title>BELGIUM: NATO chief congratulates Clinton.</title>
<headline>NATO chief congratulates Clinton.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>NATO Secretary-General Javier Solana congratulated U.S. President Bill Clinton on Wednesday on his re-election and said he looked forward to continued close cooperation within the Atlantic Alliance.</p>
<p>Solana said he looked forward to a summit of NATO leaders next year &quot;to complete the alliance's important agenda for a new security architecture in Europe&quot;.</p>
<p>The summit is expected to agree NATO's planned expansion eastwards, sign a new deal with Russia, and finalise plans for a distinct European element in the transatlantic relationship to allow the alliance to take on more peacekeeping-style missions.</p>
</text>
